# What does NOT go in the .vsix.
#
# Without this file `vsce` packages the whole folder, which means `node_modules/` — and every
# dependency here is a DEV dependency (TypeScript, the type stubs). The extension ships `out/*.js`
# and nothing else at runtime: it requires only `vscode`, which the editor provides. So the packaged
# artifact goes from tens of megabytes of compiler to a few kilobytes of extension.

src/**
node_modules/**
tsconfig.json
package-lock.json
.vscode/**
**/*.map
**/*.test.js
